-- title:
--   Regular special fibre on the pole chart, q = 2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ carrying $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((t))$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise images of the field $\mathrm{xHFunctionField}(q^2M', H)$, the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((t))$ generated by quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$, where $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ is the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ such that $q$ lies in its maximal ideal, $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, and $\varpi$ generates the maximal ideal; $K$ is an $A$-algebra over $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with $q$-expansion $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,L\,\mathrm{jq}$, and write $\mathfrak{X} = \mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A\,K\,j$, the pushout of the two maps from the mid chart to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the chart algebras (the integral closures in $K$ of $A[j]$ and of $A[j^{-1}]$), with its structure morphism $\mathrm{toBase}$ to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ characterised by: $f \in W_0$ iff $f \cdot y = x$ in $L((t))$ for some power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ nonzero modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $z$ be a point of $\mathfrak{X}$, let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section of $\mathfrak{X}$ obtained from $\varpi$ along $\mathrm{toBase}$, and assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z$. Let $y$ be a point of $X_\infty = \operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{chartAlgInf}\,A\,K\,j)$ mapping to $z$ under $\iota_\infty$, whose prime ideal is maximal and contains every element of the pole chart algebra whose image in $K$ is a nonunit of $W_0$. Let $K_0 \le K$ be the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images of the $\Gamma_0(M')$ $q$-expansion field, an $A$-algebra over $L$, with $j_0 \in K_0$ nonzero of the same $q$-expansion, let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from $\mathrm{chartAlgInf}\,A\,K_0\,j_0$ to $\mathrm{chartAlgInf}\,A\,K\,j$ compatible with the inclusion $K_0 \subseteq K$, and assume the floor model's structure morphism $\mathrm{toBase}\,A\,K_0\,j_0$ is smooth. Then, with the algebra structure on the pole chart algebra of $K$ over that of $K_0$ given by $\iota$: if the extension is unramified at every prime $\mathfrak{Q}$ of $\mathrm{chartAlgInf}\,A\,K\,j$ of height one contained in the prime of $y$, then the quotient of the stalk of $\mathfrak{X}$ at $z$ by the ideal generated by $\varpi_z$ is a regular local ring.
--
--   This is the purity step for the pole chart of the Igusa-level integral model at the prime $q = 2$: regularity of the special fibre at a closed point of the $\infty$-branch is deduced from smoothness of the floor model $X_0(M')$ over $A$ together with unramifiedness in codimension one. It feeds the corresponding statement formulated in terms of a localisation of the pole chart algebra at the prime of $y$, used in the analysis of the fibres of the Igusa model.
